    {
      "section": "conversion.faq",
      "content": {
        "headingLines": [
          "Your questions about Nimbus,",
          "answered in plain words"
        ],
        "items": [
          {
            "question": "How is pricing worked out?",
            "answer": {
              "text": "Pricing is based on the number of active users and the modules you choose. There are no hidden fees for updates or standard support. Book a short call and we will put together a quote that fits your team.",
              "linkPhrases": [
                "Book a short call"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "question": "Which tools does it connect with, and how is our data kept safe?",
            "answer": {
              "text": "Nimbus connects with common HR systems, single sign-on providers, chat apps and calendars. Data is encrypted in transit and at rest, hosted in the region you choose, and covered by regular independent audits. Our trust centre has the full details, including policies, certifications and a live status page that your IT team can review at any time before or after signing.",
              "linkPhrases": [
                "trust centre"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "question": "Can we bring our existing courses and content with us?",
            "answer": {
              "text": "Yes. You can import standard course packages, videos, documents and links, or connect content partners directly. Everything lands in one searchable library so learners never have to jump between tools to find what they need, and admins can tag, group and retire items in bulk.",
              "linkPhrases": []
            }
          },
          {
            "question": "What makes this different from a traditional learning system, and why does that matter for our people?",
            "answer": {
              "text": "Older systems were built to assign and track. Nimbus starts with the learner: a personal home feed, short content, mentoring and communities that make people want to come back. Admins still get the reporting and compliance tools they rely on, without the clunky experience that usually comes with them.",
              "linkPhrases": [
                "reporting and compliance tools"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "question": "How long does it take to get up and running?",
            "answer": {
              "text": "Most teams launch in six to eight weeks. A dedicated onboarding specialist helps with integrations, content migration and branding, and our launch playbook covers the internal comms that get people excited from the first day.",
              "linkPhrases": [
                "launch playbook"
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
